    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW266b2wAzfAJMBjD5JpGuLWE)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent; corrects #529 (already merged).\n\n## What changes\n\n- Removes the `Cmd+X` hotkey in `devonthink.lua`, so Cut works normally again in DEVONthink.\n- `Caps+x` stays the two-way toggle between selecting and highlighting, unchanged.\n- Drops the Cmd+X text and the \"Cut is lost\" caveat from the code comments. I found no README or docs text about the Cmd+X toggle; only the header comment of `devonthink.lua` mentioned it.\n- `Cmd+Z` and `Cmd+Shift+Z` are unchanged.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Reload Hammerspoon: no error in the console.\n- [ ] In DEVONthink, Cmd+X cuts selected text as usual, including with a PDF shown.\n- [ ] Caps+x toggles between selecting and highlighting on a PDF.\n- [ ] Caps+x with no PDF shown: the \"No PDF shown\" alert.\n- [ ] Cmd+Z, Cmd+Shift+Z and the colour keys still work.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCTb5QFPFZUd9wzRgq)_",
